WEBVTT

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:20.140
You're mine!

00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:24.390
Did you really think you
could get away from me?

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:29.230
She's in high school
and still catching cicadas...

00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:31.070
Hey, look!

00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:33.400
Stop that!

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.990
I've made an artificial fly
with a spring cicada before, but...

00:00:36.990 --> 00:00:39.660
I guess fish eat cicadas, too.

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:42.700
Then you should get a closer look
for when you make another one.

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:45.170
Stop!

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:50.750
Girls! Come help us make some dumplings!

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:52.670
Okay!

00:00:56.130 --> 00:01:00.720
We're currently staying at
the house my mother grew up in.

00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:19.740
<i>I had dropped something important</i>
<i>and even though I didn't know you,</i>

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:25.290
<i>You had found it and brought it back</i>
<i>to me unexpectedly this morning</i>

00:01:25.290 --> 00:01:31.040
<i>Oh yeah, I was always told to</i>
<i>write my name on important things</i>

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:36.800
<i>Or I might end up losing them somewhere</i>

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:39.760
<i>It's not (anyone's fault)</i>

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:42.470
<i>It's not (like it belongs to anyone else)</i>

00:01:42.470 --> 00:01:47.690
<i>The world will always be right there</i>

00:01:47.690 --> 00:01:50.400
<i>Let the wind (take you by the hand)</i>

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:53.190
<i>And the sky (now, breathe together)</i>

00:01:53.190 --> 00:01:55.860
<i>And let's go (it's now begun to move)</i>

00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:59.030
<i>The arrow in our hearts</i>

00:01:59.030 --> 00:02:01.950
<i>If I'm (yes, if I'm with you)</i>

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:05.330
<i>With you (yes, because I'm with you)</i>

00:02:05.330 --> 00:02:15.510
<i>We still don't know what's going to</i>
<i>happen in this future that's moving forward</i>

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:20.220
<i>And bouncing glitteringly</i>

00:02:32.230 --> 00:02:36.070
"Episode 8"
"I'm Fine Right Here"

00:02:37.570 --> 00:02:40.860
Roll, roll, roll, roll...

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:44.370
You two are going fishing at
the stream tomorrow, aren't you?

00:02:44.370 --> 00:02:45.330
Yes.

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:48.830
Then we'll have to make you some lunch.

00:02:48.830 --> 00:02:50.960
This takes me back.

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:55.170
Shinya and your grandfather used
to go fishing at the stream all the time

00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:57.510
and I'd always make them lunch.

00:02:57.510 --> 00:03:00.720
Though your grandpa mostly
went to climb the mountain.

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:04.850
Shinya's friend, Mr. Yoshinaga,
tagged along all the time, too.

00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:07.640
How nostalgic.

00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:15.110
We only had two girls, so we treated
Shinya like he was our own son.

00:03:15.110 --> 00:03:18.280
Then will Grandpa go fishing
with us tomorrow...?

00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:20.280
Thank you for thinking of him, dear,

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:25.120
but he's hurt his back
and won't be able to go.

00:03:26.490 --> 00:03:28.950
Dumplings complete!

00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:32.620
Then will you go take this
to your grandfather's room?

00:03:33.710 --> 00:03:35.460
S-Sure.

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:39.590
Grandpa.

00:03:42.050 --> 00:03:47.970
Um... We made some dumplings. Here you go.

00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:49.600
Mm.

00:03:58.070 --> 00:04:02.360
Do you not get along
with your grandpa, Hiyori?

00:04:02.360 --> 00:04:05.740
Yeah... He's really quiet
and not very expressive,

00:04:05.740 --> 00:04:08.410
so I have no idea what he's thinking.

00:04:08.410 --> 00:04:10.750
He sort of reminds me of you.

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:11.710
Huh?

00:04:11.710 --> 00:04:14.210
Don't worry.

00:04:14.210 --> 00:04:16.250
Your grandpa's very happy.

00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:18.340
R-Really?

00:04:18.340 --> 00:04:23.300
Yes. He's been looking
forward to having you two over.

00:04:27.640 --> 00:04:34.310
But honestly... Why are all of the
dumplings you made all different sizes?

00:04:34.310 --> 00:04:38.730
W-Well, I thought that'd be more fun.

00:04:38.730 --> 00:04:41.110
They're going to cook unevenly.

00:04:41.110 --> 00:04:44.400
It's fine. They're still edible.

00:04:48.370 --> 00:04:53.000
It's funny hearing my mom talk to
my grandma because she sounds kiddy.

00:04:53.000 --> 00:05:00.000
Yeah, it was really cute.
She's usually so calm and smiley.

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:06.340
Yeah... She used to
get angry and cry a lot.

00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:10.180
Why won't you just listen to me?

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:13.980
Oh, my. I sorta want to see that.

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:20.400
Ever since my dad died,
I've only seen her smiling.

00:05:23.530 --> 00:05:27.410
Oh, yeah! Look at this!

00:05:27.410 --> 00:05:29.450
I bought a rain poncho!

00:05:29.450 --> 00:05:32.870
A poncho? That's probably
going to be hard to move in.

00:05:32.870 --> 00:05:35.660
You're supposed to say it's cute!

00:05:39.130 --> 00:05:41.800
What a great day to be at the stream!

00:05:41.800 --> 00:05:44.710
Can I cast now? Hey, can I?

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:48.340
Hold on. I brought some equipment
to help us go into the river.

00:05:48.340 --> 00:05:49.840
Oho?

00:05:57.730 --> 00:05:59.150
Try going in.

00:05:59.150 --> 00:06:02.650
Huh? Are you sure?
It doesn't seem very waterproof.

00:06:02.650 --> 00:06:04.650
Don't worry; you'll be fine.

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:15.870
So cowd! Water's coming in...

00:06:17.330 --> 00:06:21.460
But now it's getting sorta warm.

00:06:21.460 --> 00:06:24.840
These things that look like
shin guards are called gaiters.

00:06:24.840 --> 00:06:27.420
They help keep heat in,
so even if water gets in,

00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:31.430
it'll make it our body temperature,
and keep you from getting cold.

00:06:31.430 --> 00:06:35.850
Ooh! Now I feel like I can go anywhere!

00:06:35.850 --> 00:06:38.440
Wait, wait, wait. Koharu! Shh!

00:06:38.440 --> 00:06:41.600
You're going to scare the fish,
so you need to be quiet!

00:06:43.650 --> 00:06:45.530
We're going to be fishing for char today.

00:06:45.530 --> 00:06:48.240
In Japanese, they're called <i>iwana</i>.
Do you know why?

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:50.240
Hm... they're a rock type
because <i>iwa </i>means rock?

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:51.950
"Resistant against physical attacks!!"

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:51.950
Hm... they're a rock type
because <i>iwa </i>means rock?

00:06:51.950 --> 00:06:54.330
"Resistant against physical attacks!!"

00:06:51.950 --> 00:06:54.330
We're not talking about a game here.

00:06:54.330 --> 00:06:54.990
We're not talking about a game here.

00:06:54.990 --> 00:06:57.450
They're called <i>iwana </i>because
they're fish that live in between rocks.

00:06:57.450 --> 00:06:58.790
"<i>Iwana </i>(Char)"

00:06:57.450 --> 00:06:58.790
They're called <i>iwana </i>because
they're fish that live in between rocks.

00:06:58.790 --> 00:07:02.500
"<i>Iwana </i>(Char)"

00:06:58.790 --> 00:07:02.500
They usually hide under rocks
and wait for insects that get

00:07:02.500 --> 00:07:04.960
"<i>Iwana </i>(Char)"

00:07:02.500 --> 00:07:04.960
carried upstream or fall from rocks.

00:07:04.960 --> 00:07:09.130
That's why it's said that if you want
to catch <i>iwana</i>, aim for some rocks.

00:07:09.130 --> 00:07:10.470
Huh...

00:07:10.470 --> 00:07:15.760
So yeah, maybe them being
a rock type isn't too far off.

00:07:15.760 --> 00:07:18.600
Okay, first. Let's aim for some rocks.

00:07:18.600 --> 00:07:20.730
Aye, got it!

00:07:20.730 --> 00:07:23.270
Okay, start walking gently from here.

00:07:23.270 --> 00:07:25.900
Uh-huh.

00:07:25.900 --> 00:07:29.110
Keep crouching so
the fish can't see you...

00:07:29.110 --> 00:07:32.070
And try casting your artificial fly like
you're trying to land on one of the rocks.

00:07:32.070 --> 00:07:33.160
Okay.

00:07:33.160 --> 00:07:37.450
So the artificial fly falls onto the
surface of the water after it lands.

00:07:40.830 --> 00:07:43.460
Yeah, you there you go.

00:07:43.460 --> 00:07:46.130
Chomp!

00:07:46.130 --> 00:07:47.590
Now, chomp!

00:07:47.590 --> 00:07:50.090
Chomp!

00:07:50.090 --> 00:07:52.550
Chomp!

00:07:52.550 --> 00:07:54.550
Chomp!

00:07:54.550 --> 00:07:56.390
Chomp!

00:07:56.390 --> 00:07:59.850
Aw, no chomp. Let's try
casting a couple more times.

00:07:59.850 --> 00:08:01.850
O-Okay...

00:08:04.230 --> 00:08:05.900
Chomp!

00:08:05.900 --> 00:08:08.360
Come on! Chomp!

00:08:08.360 --> 00:08:09.780
Chomp...

00:08:11.030 --> 00:08:13.410
Wh-What's wrong?

00:08:15.490 --> 00:08:21.790
I-I mean... You keep acting
like a fish and it's so funny.

00:08:25.920 --> 00:08:28.290
Let's just go to our next spot.

00:08:28.290 --> 00:08:30.670
Huh? Hey, wait!

00:08:30.670 --> 00:08:34.220
You made a ruckus,
so all the fish are guarded now.

00:08:34.220 --> 00:08:36.850
What?!

00:08:42.890 --> 00:08:45.350
The fish in mountain
streams don't migrate,

00:08:45.350 --> 00:08:49.570
so staying in one spot doesn't make sense.

00:08:49.570 --> 00:08:51.940
And that's why...

00:08:51.940 --> 00:08:56.320
...they also say to catch
<i>iwana </i>with your feet.

00:08:56.320 --> 00:08:58.530
We're going to be walking a lot today.

00:09:00.700 --> 00:09:02.580
Bring it on!

00:09:44.370 --> 00:09:46.620
I just can't get the timing down.

00:09:46.620 --> 00:09:50.340
It's harder to get the flow here than
the other place because of the current...

00:09:54.010 --> 00:09:59.260
Hiyori keeps catching some. I'm jealous.

00:09:59.260 --> 00:10:02.390
Wait, you're letting them go?

00:10:02.390 --> 00:10:05.600
Oh, right. I guess every
other time we've been fishing,

00:10:05.600 --> 00:10:08.100
we'd eat the fish we caught.

00:10:08.100 --> 00:10:09.400
Look here.

00:10:09.400 --> 00:10:14.070
I'm using a barbless fly to fish today,
meaning it doesn't have the jagged end.

00:10:14.070 --> 00:10:16.440
How is it different
without the jagged end?

00:10:16.440 --> 00:10:21.200
This makes it easier to get the
hook off and the fish don't get as hurt.

00:10:21.200 --> 00:10:23.160
I see.

00:10:23.160 --> 00:10:27.160
When you release them, you want to keep
them in the water as much as possible.

00:10:27.160 --> 00:10:31.460
You want to chill your hands in the water
and then quickly remove the hook.

00:10:31.460 --> 00:10:35.920
If you take too long,
you'll just weaken the fish.

00:10:39.130 --> 00:10:43.850
It's actually uncommon for people
who fly fish to eat what they catch.

00:10:43.850 --> 00:10:47.890
Huh? You catch them
but don't eat them? Why?

00:10:47.890 --> 00:10:50.310
There are plenty of reasons...

00:10:50.310 --> 00:10:55.400
But I think the biggest reason is because
people mostly go fly fishing in streams.

00:10:55.400 --> 00:10:59.320
Unlike the ocean, there aren't
that many fish in the streams.

00:10:59.320 --> 00:11:01.450
There are plenty of rivers where if we

00:11:01.450 --> 00:11:05.080
took all the fish we caught home with us,
there wouldn't be any more fish.

00:11:05.080 --> 00:11:10.540
That's why I think most of us
tend to release them.

00:11:10.540 --> 00:11:12.880
So it's for the fish?

00:11:12.880 --> 00:11:14.840
Hm...

00:11:14.840 --> 00:11:17.630
No, it's for ourselves.

00:11:17.630 --> 00:11:21.840
Because we want to come back here
to fish the next year and the year after.

00:11:21.840 --> 00:11:26.720
We want them to keep growing
so we can catch even larger fish.

00:11:28.770 --> 00:11:32.810
I basically just want to enjoy fishing...

00:11:32.810 --> 00:11:34.900
So it's just my selfishness.

00:11:37.730 --> 00:11:41.150
Well, whenever I hook one
and drag them out of the water,

00:11:41.150 --> 00:11:45.030
I feel like we should eat them.

00:11:45.030 --> 00:11:49.120
Of course, I'd never take too many home.
Just what we're going to eat.

00:11:49.120 --> 00:11:52.620
Yeah. And I think that's fine for you.

00:11:52.620 --> 00:11:57.750
Hup. But I guess you'll have
to actually catch one first.

00:11:57.750 --> 00:11:59.630
And I will!

00:11:59.630 --> 00:12:00.590
Yeah, sure.

00:12:00.590 --> 00:12:02.380
I totally will!

00:12:02.380 --> 00:12:04.800
Be careful there.

00:12:09.270 --> 00:12:11.060
Hm...

00:12:11.060 --> 00:12:15.560
My artificial fly's not floating
anymore. I need to bring it up.

00:12:23.320 --> 00:12:26.830
I... I got one!

00:12:30.910 --> 00:12:33.000
Don't figure me out!

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:34.540
Koharu!

00:12:38.250 --> 00:12:40.300
I...

00:12:41.420 --> 00:12:44.430
I did it!

00:12:44.430 --> 00:12:46.890
Good job! That's amazing!

00:12:46.890 --> 00:12:48.510
Yeah! It was amazing!

00:12:48.510 --> 00:12:53.060
I basically gave up and was pulling up
my line and then felt a tug!

00:12:53.060 --> 00:12:54.140
I felt a tug!

00:12:54.140 --> 00:12:57.110
Yeah! Congratulations, Koharu.

00:12:59.230 --> 00:13:01.940
Thank you for eating my artificial fly...

00:13:01.940 --> 00:13:03.530
Iwagoro.

00:13:03.530 --> 00:13:06.740
And now, she's attached.

00:13:06.740 --> 00:13:08.990
Okay, we better prep it.

00:13:08.990 --> 00:13:11.490
Iwagoro!

00:13:11.490 --> 00:13:14.160
If we don't do this now, it'll go bad.

00:13:14.160 --> 00:13:16.210
I see...

00:13:16.210 --> 00:13:20.590
Don't worry, Iwagoro. I'll make
sure we eat you in a delicious way.

00:13:22.920 --> 00:13:24.920
Hiyori?

00:13:24.920 --> 00:13:27.720
I smell lightning clouds.

00:13:33.930 --> 00:13:36.850
You're right! Are you psychic?!

00:13:36.850 --> 00:13:38.610
Let's call it for today.

00:13:38.610 --> 00:13:42.820
Aw, but I want to fish some more...

00:13:42.820 --> 00:13:45.780
Whoa, I really heard some thunder.

00:13:45.780 --> 00:13:49.240
Koharu! Lower your rod!
Lightning will strike.

00:13:50.950 --> 00:13:53.080
Let's hurry to the mountain hut.

00:13:53.080 --> 00:13:54.160
Okay!

00:13:54.160 --> 00:13:58.750
Um... Where did I put my rain poncho...?

00:14:10.140 --> 00:14:13.810
Koharu, you okay?

00:14:13.810 --> 00:14:15.520
Or not?!

00:14:17.190 --> 00:14:21.060
I forgot my rain poncho
back at your grandma's house...

00:14:21.060 --> 00:14:24.780
Jeez... You should've told me earlier.

00:14:24.780 --> 00:14:26.740
Where's my towel...?

00:14:26.740 --> 00:14:30.870
But... I'm the big sister...

00:14:30.870 --> 00:14:35.120
I'm not sure how
this is big sister like...

00:14:35.120 --> 00:14:39.540
I'm sorry I caused you trouble.

00:14:41.290 --> 00:14:43.840
I'm just used to stuff
like this happening.

00:14:43.840 --> 00:14:46.460
Wait, one sec.
I'll get a change of clothes out.

00:14:46.460 --> 00:14:48.930
Thanks...

00:14:50.760 --> 00:14:53.930
It's still summer,
so she'll probably be fine.

00:14:55.770 --> 00:14:58.730
Or not...

00:14:58.730 --> 00:15:02.110
Hello, Issei?

00:15:02.110 --> 00:15:05.780
Yes. Koharu caught a cold.

00:15:05.780 --> 00:15:08.650
All right. I'll head right over.

00:15:08.650 --> 00:15:11.910
Huh? But I thought you
had to work until today.

00:15:11.910 --> 00:15:17.000
I'll talk to my work.
I should be there by evening.

00:15:17.000 --> 00:15:21.040
Okay. Be careful.

00:15:21.040 --> 00:15:24.960
Koharu, your dad is heading right over.

00:15:24.960 --> 00:15:26.590
Okay...

00:15:31.050 --> 00:15:33.140
Hiyori...

00:15:34.470 --> 00:15:37.350
I'm so sorry...

00:15:37.350 --> 00:15:39.730
Just sleep for now.

00:15:41.690 --> 00:15:44.650
I'll be a good girl...

00:15:44.650 --> 00:15:47.280
So don't hate me.

00:15:51.700 --> 00:15:54.160
Don't worry.

00:15:54.160 --> 00:15:57.200
I don't hate you...

00:16:00.620 --> 00:16:04.130
Hello, dear. Did you go shopping?

00:16:05.170 --> 00:16:10.420
Oh, what's all of this?
You bought so much fruit.

00:16:11.630 --> 00:16:14.840
Ah, you wanted Koharu to eat them.

00:16:14.840 --> 00:16:15.680
This, too.

00:16:15.680 --> 00:16:16.720
My, that looks delicious.

00:16:16.720 --> 00:16:18.810
And this.

00:16:22.730 --> 00:16:25.310
How's Koharu doing?

00:16:25.310 --> 00:16:26.940
She took some medicine and is asleep now.

00:16:26.940 --> 00:16:31.780
I see. Well, her fever isn't too bad,
so when she feels like eating again,

00:16:31.780 --> 00:16:34.070
I'll make her some rice porridge.

00:16:34.070 --> 00:16:38.740
We need to hurry up and
cook that char Koharu caught, too.

00:16:38.740 --> 00:16:43.080
Grandma, could you teach me how to cook?

00:16:46.040 --> 00:16:49.210
Hm. Looks like there aren't any parasites.

00:16:49.210 --> 00:16:52.300
Once you scale the fish with the knife,

00:16:52.300 --> 00:16:55.970
use a paper towel to soak up any
excess moisture, and we'll chop it up.

00:16:55.970 --> 00:16:58.220
O-Okay.

00:17:00.810 --> 00:17:05.600
With normal miso soup, we first let
the ingredients cook, turn off the heat,

00:17:05.600 --> 00:17:08.570
and then add in the miso to let it melt...

00:17:08.570 --> 00:17:14.320
But for this, we want the miso to soak
into the char, so we cook them together.

00:17:14.320 --> 00:17:18.780
We'll let it stew for about
30 minutes to an hour.

00:17:18.780 --> 00:17:19.780
Is that it?

00:17:19.780 --> 00:17:23.120
Yes. Easy, isn't it?

00:17:26.370 --> 00:17:32.590
I know! Once Koharu feels better, we can
all go to the botanical garden nearby.

00:17:32.590 --> 00:17:36.680
The summer flowers will be in full bloom.
We can make some lunch!

00:17:36.680 --> 00:17:39.970
I'll help make some.

00:17:39.970 --> 00:17:44.480
Uh, Dad?! What's that face for?

00:17:48.440 --> 00:17:50.570
Mommy...

00:17:53.900 --> 00:17:59.570
Good morning, Koharu. I cut up
some apples for you. Want some?

00:17:59.570 --> 00:18:01.240
I eat!

00:18:01.240 --> 00:18:04.790
I'm asking your sister.

00:18:04.790 --> 00:18:10.630
Aw, quit pouting. You're always
so grumpy when you wake up.

00:18:10.630 --> 00:18:15.470
Nuh-uh. I'm mad because you
wouldn't come see me for days...

00:18:15.470 --> 00:18:20.510
I'm sorry, dear. But Natsuki's
fever just wouldn't go down...

00:18:22.100 --> 00:18:24.140
Well, I don't care.

00:18:29.940 --> 00:18:33.980
Come on, smile!

00:18:35.190 --> 00:18:38.450
Natty, too! Natty, too!

00:18:42.530 --> 00:18:44.200
What a weird face!

00:18:44.200 --> 00:18:47.580
Yup. You're the cutest
in the whole wide world.

00:18:59.090 --> 00:19:02.100
Huh? Oh, you were awake, Koharu?

00:19:02.100 --> 00:19:05.310
No... I just woke up.

00:19:06.390 --> 00:19:09.940
I think I woke up because I'm hungry...

00:19:09.940 --> 00:19:12.980
Perfect timing, then.

00:19:12.980 --> 00:19:17.440
Here's some char soup.
My grandma taught me how to make it.

00:19:17.440 --> 00:19:19.530
You made this, Hiyori?

00:19:19.530 --> 00:19:20.410
Yup.

00:19:20.410 --> 00:19:23.410
Wow... Thank you.

00:19:23.410 --> 00:19:25.410
Thanks for the food.

00:19:36.300 --> 00:19:38.670
It's so good.

00:19:41.010 --> 00:19:43.890
I can totally taste you, Iwagoro.

00:19:43.890 --> 00:19:45.600
Do you have to say it like that?

00:19:45.600 --> 00:19:48.680
Mm... Yum.

00:19:50.270 --> 00:19:52.190
Koharu, are you okay?!

00:19:52.190 --> 00:19:55.820
Daddy! You got here fast. Where's my gift?

00:19:56.980 --> 00:20:00.280
Thank goodness you seem okay...

00:20:00.280 --> 00:20:02.700
I ate Iwagoro, so I feel all better now.

00:20:02.700 --> 00:20:06.490
Of course! Iwagoro... Wait, who?

00:20:10.870 --> 00:20:13.880
Koharu, are you okay being up?

00:20:13.880 --> 00:20:18.380
Yup! Actually, I slept
too much so I'm tired now.

00:20:18.380 --> 00:20:21.470
I guess I ended up
causing everyone trouble.

00:20:21.470 --> 00:20:25.010
I'll be my usual cheerful self tomorrow!

00:20:26.680 --> 00:20:32.270
You worried us, but you didn't trouble us.

00:20:32.270 --> 00:20:35.480
Say, Koharu.

00:20:35.480 --> 00:20:39.070
Whenever things are rough,
it's okay to complain...

00:20:39.070 --> 00:20:42.900
And if you're ever sad, it's okay to cry.

00:20:42.900 --> 00:20:45.320
I mean... be...

00:20:45.320 --> 00:20:49.580
Because we're family...

00:20:51.540 --> 00:20:53.330
Yeah.

00:20:55.330 --> 00:20:57.170
Yeah.

00:21:08.010 --> 00:21:11.560
Huh? Fireworks?

00:21:11.560 --> 00:21:15.650
Oh, yeah. Today's the fireworks festival.

00:21:15.650 --> 00:21:20.900
It's actually a pretty big festival
with plenty of food stalls and stuff.

00:21:22.690 --> 00:21:29.780
And if I wasn't sick,
you could've gone... I-I'm so sorry.

00:21:29.780 --> 00:21:33.580
Nah, I hate crowds anyway, so it's fine.

00:21:36.580 --> 00:21:38.630
I'm fine right here.

00:21:40.130 --> 00:21:41.800
Yeah...

00:21:41.800 --> 00:21:46.050
Me, too. I'm fine right here.

00:21:46.050 --> 00:21:49.390
By the way, there's a huge
botanical garden nearby,

00:21:49.390 --> 00:21:52.890
and we were talking about how
we should all go when you feel better.

00:21:52.890 --> 00:21:54.980
Wait, really? I wanna go!

00:21:54.980 --> 00:21:56.980
We're all going to make lunch.

00:21:56.980 --> 00:22:03.110
Ooh, I can't wait to cook!
I wonder what I should make.

00:22:03.110 --> 00:22:07.820
Yeah. I rely on you a lot... Big Sis.

00:22:07.820 --> 00:22:11.580
Huh? What did you just say?

00:22:11.580 --> 00:22:13.240
I didn't say anything.

00:22:13.240 --> 00:22:16.410
Hey, say that one more time!
Please! Come on!

00:22:16.410 --> 00:22:18.460
I didn't say anything, okay?

00:22:18.460 --> 00:22:21.090
Aw, come on!

00:22:30.220 --> 00:22:32.810
<i>Even if you don't say anything</i>

00:22:32.810 --> 00:22:38.560
<i>I know how you're feeling and</i>
<i>when you're lying or telling the truth</i>

00:22:38.560 --> 00:22:41.190
<i>Even if you don't do anything</i>

00:22:41.190 --> 00:22:46.190
<i>Just being next to you</i>
<i>makes the day brighter</i>

00:22:46.190 --> 00:22:50.410
<i>The reason I've always loved the ocean</i>

00:22:50.410 --> 00:22:55.160
<i>Is because you were always by my side</i>

00:22:55.160 --> 00:22:58.370
<i>The way we laugh is becoming similar</i>

00:22:58.370 --> 00:23:03.500
<i>It's almost like we're cider</i>

00:23:03.500 --> 00:23:07.720
<i>Bubble, bubble, our laughter combines</i>

00:23:07.720 --> 00:23:12.010
<i>Bubble, bubble, then floats up</i>
<i>and pops together</i>

00:23:12.010 --> 00:23:20.270
<i>We gather up the light and</i>
<i>gain even more precious things</i>

00:23:20.270 --> 00:23:24.520
<i>Bubble, bubble, our laughter combines</i>

00:23:24.520 --> 00:23:28.860
<i>Bubble, bubble, then floats up</i>
<i>and pops together</i>

00:23:28.860 --> 00:23:33.830
<i>May a present where we can</i>
<i>laugh about the past and future</i>

00:23:33.830 --> 00:23:39.960
<i>Always be right here</i>

00:23:41.500 --> 00:23:46.500
<i>May a present where we can</i>
<i>laugh about the past and future</i>

00:23:46.500 --> 00:23:52.890
<i>Always be right here</i>

00:23:55.010 --> 00:23:55.350
"Next Time"

00:23:55.350 --> 00:23:58.770
"Next Time"
If you wanna catch <i>iwana</i>, aim for
some rocks! Catch <i>iwana </i>with your feet.

00:23:58.770 --> 00:24:00.310
"Next Time"
Are there any more sayings like that?

00:24:00.310 --> 00:24:03.440
"Next Time"
Well, they call landlocked salmon
the queen of the mountain stream.

00:24:03.440 --> 00:24:08.030
"Next Time"
That's so cool! Then I guess we can
call you the Fly-Fishing Queen, Hiyori!

00:24:08.030 --> 00:24:09.940
"Next Time"
That's so embarrassing.
